From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net airoha strip the DSA tag after the TX ring check

airoha_dev_xmit() moved the MTK DSA tag into the descriptor (memmove plus
__skb_pull, or a rewrite of the TPID) before checking the TX ring for
room.  When the ring was full it returned NETDEV_TX_BUSY with the skb
already changed; the stack resends the same skb and the second pass took
the real EtherType for a tag, cut four more bytes and put garbage into
SP_TAG.  Several netdev queues share one hardware ring, so another queue
can hit a full ring while its own txq is still running.

Take the tag once the frame is sure to be queued, under q->lock.  Same
issue fixed in the X-WRT airoha driver ("Check locked TX ring capacity
before DSA conversion").

Signed-off-by: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -2992,13 +2992,11 @@ static netdev_tx_t airoha_dev_xmit(struc
 	 */
 	txq_idx = skb_get_queue_mapping(skb) % AIROHA_NUM_TX_RING;
 	qid = airoha_qdma_get_txq(qdma, txq_idx);
-	tag = airoha_get_dsa_tag(skb, netdev);
 
 	msg0 = FIELD_PREP(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_CHAN_MASK,
 			  txq_idx / AIROHA_NUM_QOS_QUEUES) |
 	       FIELD_PREP(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_QUEUE_MASK,
-			  txq_idx % AIROHA_NUM_QOS_QUEUES) |
-	       FIELD_PREP(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_SP_TAG_MASK, tag);
+			  txq_idx % AIROHA_NUM_QOS_QUEUES);
 	if (skb->ip_summed == CHECKSUM_PARTIAL)
 		msg0 |= FIELD_PREP(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_TCO_MASK, 1) |
 			FIELD_PREP(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_UCO_MASK, 1) |
@@ -3045,6 +3043,14 @@ static netdev_tx_t airoha_dev_xmit(struc
 		return NETDEV_TX_BUSY;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Move the DSA tag into the descriptor only once the frame will be
+	 * queued: the stack resends a NETDEV_TX_BUSY skb and a second pass
+	 * would strip it again.
+	 */
+	tag = airoha_get_dsa_tag(skb, netdev);
+	msg0 |= FIELD_PREP(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_SP_TAG_MASK, tag);
+
 	e = list_first_entry(&q->tx_list, struct airoha_queue_entry,
 			     list);
 	len = skb_headlen(skb);
